WEBVTT

00:00.260 --> 00:02.628
- [Voiceover] Derek sent a
chain letter to his friends,

00:02.628 --> 00:05.321
asking them to forward the
letter to more friends.

00:05.321 --> 00:07.504
The group of people who
receive the email gains

00:07.504 --> 00:10.662
9/10 of its size every three weeks,

00:10.662 --> 00:12.867
and can be modeled by a function, P,

00:12.867 --> 00:16.280
which depends on the
amount of time, t in weeks.

00:16.280 --> 00:19.241
Derek initially sent the
chain letter to 40 friends.

00:19.241 --> 00:21.539
Write a function that
models the group of people

00:21.539 --> 00:24.047
who receive the email t weeks

00:24.047 --> 00:26.763
since Derek initially
sent the chain letter.

00:26.763 --> 00:29.758
So pause the video if you
wanna have a go at this.

00:29.758 --> 00:31.906
All right, now the way I'd
like to think about this,

00:31.906 --> 00:33.508
let's just gonna table

00:33.508 --> 00:37.181
with values for t

00:37.181 --> 00:39.422
and our function P

00:39.422 --> 00:41.988
which is a function of t.

00:41.988 --> 00:43.729
For some values that we can just pull out

00:43.729 --> 00:45.343
of the description here.

00:45.343 --> 00:48.442
So when t is zero, when
it's been zero weeks

00:48.442 --> 00:50.659
since Derek initially
sent the chain letter,

00:50.659 --> 00:52.470
how many people have gotten it?

00:52.470 --> 00:53.086
Well, they tell us.

00:53.086 --> 00:55.268
He initially, Derek initially sent

00:55.268 --> 00:57.404
the chain letter to 40 friends.

00:57.404 --> 00:58.925
So t equals zero.

00:58.925 --> 01:01.653
P of t or P of zero is 40.

01:01.653 --> 01:04.486
Now, what's an interesting time period?

01:04.486 --> 01:06.007
It says that the email,
the number of people

01:06.007 --> 01:08.491
who receive the email gains 9/10

01:08.491 --> 01:11.950
or increases by 9/10 every three weeks,

01:11.950 --> 01:13.564
every three weeks.

01:13.564 --> 01:15.770
So after three weeks,

01:15.770 --> 01:17.453
so three weeks have gone by.

01:17.453 --> 01:20.146
So I'm just adding three to t.

01:20.146 --> 01:22.004
What is P of t going to be?

01:22.004 --> 01:25.321
Well, they tell us it's going
to gain 9/10 of its size.

01:25.321 --> 01:27.981
So it's going to be 40

01:27.981 --> 01:32.981
plus 9/10 times 40

01:33.183 --> 01:35.505
which is going to be equal to, what?

01:35.505 --> 01:37.741
Well, that's equal to 40.

01:37.741 --> 01:39.006
We factor out our 40.

01:39.006 --> 01:43.162
40 times one plus 9/10

01:43.162 --> 01:46.598
or you could say this
is equal to 40 times,

01:46.598 --> 01:51.184
whoops, 40 times 1.9.

01:51.184 --> 01:52.206
Another way of thinking about it,

01:52.206 --> 01:54.678
after three weeks, we've grown 90%.

01:54.678 --> 01:56.478
That's another way of saying
that the number of people

01:56.478 --> 01:59.568
who receive the email
gains 9/10 of its size.

01:59.568 --> 02:02.308
You could say the group of
people who receive the email

02:02.308 --> 02:06.303
grows 90% every three weeks.

02:06.303 --> 02:08.451
And so if we go another three weeks,

02:08.451 --> 02:09.856
so plus another three weeks,

02:09.856 --> 02:10.838
I could say, well, let me just write this,

02:10.838 --> 02:12.231
this is six weeks.

02:12.231 --> 02:14.739
Well, how many people would
have received the email?

02:14.739 --> 02:16.097
It was going to be this number.

02:16.097 --> 02:18.651
It's going to be grown another 90%.

02:18.651 --> 02:21.240
So we're gonna multiply
it times 1.9 again.

02:21.240 --> 02:22.691
So it's going to be 40

02:22.691 --> 02:26.116
times 1.9 times 1.9.

02:26.116 --> 02:28.252
We're gonna grow by another 9/10.

02:28.252 --> 02:30.817
Growing by 9/10 is the
same thing as multiplying

02:30.817 --> 02:33.011
by one and 9/10.

02:33.011 --> 02:34.439
The one is what you already are.

02:34.439 --> 02:36.517
Then you're growing by another 9/10.

02:36.517 --> 02:38.433
So this is the same thing as 40

02:38.433 --> 02:41.811
times 1.9 squared.

02:41.811 --> 02:44.690
We go another three weeks,

02:44.690 --> 02:45.816
nine weeks.

02:45.816 --> 02:47.492
We're gonna grow another 90%.

02:47.492 --> 02:48.955
So you're gonna multiply it by,

02:48.955 --> 02:50.092
you're gonna take this number

02:50.092 --> 02:51.938
and multiply by 1.9 again

02:51.938 --> 02:55.851
which is going to be
1.9 to the third power.

02:55.851 --> 02:58.056
And so what's going on over here?

02:58.056 --> 02:59.751
Well, we can see some
exponential function.

02:59.751 --> 03:01.318
We have our initial value.

03:01.318 --> 03:03.849
And every three weeks,
we're multiplying by 1.9.

03:03.849 --> 03:06.113
So 1.9 would be our common ratio.

03:06.113 --> 03:11.113
So we could say that P of t is
equal to our initial value 40

03:11.295 --> 03:14.309
times our common ratio 1.9.

03:14.309 --> 03:18.438
And we multiply by 1.9 every three weeks.

03:18.438 --> 03:19.402
So we could just say,

03:19.402 --> 03:22.199
how many three week
periods have passed by?

03:22.199 --> 03:25.357
Well, we will take t
and divide it by three.

03:25.357 --> 03:27.342
T divided by three is a
number of three week periods

03:27.342 --> 03:28.886
that have gone by.

03:28.886 --> 03:29.664
And there you have it.

03:29.664 --> 03:31.487
And notice, t equals zero,

03:31.487 --> 03:34.366
1.9 to the zeroth power is one

03:34.366 --> 03:35.759
so 40 times one.

03:35.759 --> 03:39.485
T equals three, that's gonna
be 1.9 to the first power,

03:39.485 --> 03:40.600
three over three.

03:40.600 --> 03:43.943
And so we're gonna grow by
90% and so on and so forth.

03:43.943 --> 03:46.376
So feeling pretty good about this.
